 "id": "2026-11-28-week-above-2c",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Seven straight days at two degrees of warming. Is the Paris limit already broken?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Europe's Copernicus climate service says the global average temperature stayed more than two degrees Celsius above pre-industrial levels from November eighteenth to twenty-fourth. Copernicus says no week like that is on record."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Earlier spells above two degrees were short, reports say. Two days in November twenty twenty-three. Four days in February twenty twenty-four. This November, the mark was hit on ten days in total. The data are still preliminary, Copernicus says."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "So is the Paris limit broken? No, says Copernicus climate lead Samantha Burgess. The treaty counts warming over many years, not days. She calls the week a stark preview of where our climate is headed. Scientists link the spike to a strong El Niño on top of long-term warming."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will next year break the global heat record? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
